)\n .pre-commit-config.yaml | 2 +-\n 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)\nd7def7d Speed up array appends (#666)\n CHANGELOG.md                |  4 +++\n tests/test_array_appends.py | 74 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n tomlkit/items.py            |  9 +++++-\n 3 files changed, 86 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)\n9e83543 chore: ask contributors and agents to check for duplicate open PRs\n .github/pull_request_template.md | 27 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++-\n 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)\n7ab0c79 Resolve remaining API documentation reference warnings (#667)\n docs/api.rst   |  9 ++++++++-\n docs/conf.py   | 17 +++++++++++++++++\n tomlkit/api.py |  3 ++-\n 3 files changed, 27 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)\n004fce6 Reject datetime strings in date factory (#673)\n tests/test_api.py | 13 +++++++++++++\n tomlkit/api.py    |  2 +-\n 2 files changed, 14 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)\n0092bdd [pre-commit.ci] pre-commit autoupdate (#674)\n .pre-commit-config.yaml | 2 +-\n 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)\ne781ee0 Copy trivia in _new so arithmetic results cannot mutate the original item (#683)\n CHANGELOG.md        |  4 ++++\n tests/test_items.py | 25 +++++++++++++++++++++++++\n tomlkit/items.py    | 12 ++++++------\n 3 files changed, 35 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)\neec255e chore(deps): bump certifi from 2024.7.4 to 2026.10.19 (#684)\n uv.lock | 6 +++---\n 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)\n9f5b2f9 chore(deps): bump certifi from 2024.7.4 to 2026.10.19 in /docs (#685)\n docs/requirements.txt | 8 +++-----\n 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)\n6421a6e chore(deps): bump virtualenv from 21.14.8 to 21.14.13 (#689)\n uv.lock | 8 ++++----\n 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)\ncd46e5d Keep the Python 3.9 Linux job on Ubuntu 24.04 (#681)\n .github/workflows/tests.yml | 7 +++++++\n 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)\n10fbd37 Fix regression in String.from_raw and improve documentation (#658)\n tomlkit/api.py   | 10 ++++++----\n tomlkit/items.py | 27 +++++++++++++--------------\n 2 files changed, 19 insertions(+), 18 deletions(-)\neddd27e chore(deps): bump urllib3 from 2.6.3 to 2.8.0 (#670)\n uv.lock | 33 +++++----------------------------\n 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 28 deletions(-)\n2a12a36 chore(deps): bump soupsieve from 2.8.4 to 2.9 (#669)\n docs/requirements.txt |  6 ++--\n uv.lock               | 82 ++++++++++++++++++++++-----------------------------\n 2 files changed, 39 insertions(+), 49 deletions(-)\ndiff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md\nindex abf9a769..00914bb0 100644\n--- a/CHANGELOG.md\n+++ b/CHANGELOG.md\n@@ -2,21 +2,38 @@\n \n ## [Unreleased]\n \n+## [0.15.3] - 2026-11-24\n+\n ### Changed\n \n-- Speed up looking up and replacing keys in tables: string lookups no longer build a temporary key, and replacing an existing value no longer scans every key in the table, which made updating many keys of a large table quadratic.\n-- Speed up repeated array appends by keeping existing indexes instead of rebuilding them.\n-- Speed up creating string values and keys, e.g. when building a document from Python data and dumping it: strings are escaped in one pass instead of per character, and the escape and bare-key character sets are built once.\n+- Speed up looking up and replacing keys in tables: string lookups no longer build a temporary key, and replacing an existing value no longer scans every key in the table, which made updating many keys of a large table quadratic. ([#704](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/704))\n+- Speed up repeated array appends by keeping existing indexes instead of rebuilding them. ([#666](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/666))\n+- Speed up creating string values and keys, e.g. when building a document from Python data and dumping it: strings are escaped in one pass instead of per character, and the escape and bare-key character sets are built once. ([#709](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/709))\n+- `comment()`, `Item.comment()` and `Array.add_line(..., comment=...)` now raise `ValueError` for control characters that TOML forbids in comments (anything but tab, plus `DEL`), including a bare carriage return; `comment()` still accepts LF and CRLF line breaks. Previously such comments were written out and produced a document that could not be parsed back. ([#705](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/705))\n+- `date()` now raises `ValueError` when given a datetime string such as `\"1979-05-13T12:34:56\"` instead of returning a datetime. ([#673](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/673))\n+- `Array.sort()` now reorders the serialized values too, keeping the array's formatting and comments in place; previously `list.sort()` only reordered the Python list, so `dumps()` still wrote the old order. ([#644](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/644))\n \n ### Fixed\n \n - `dumps(..., sort_keys=True)` now sorts the keys of a parsed document recursively, matching the behavior on a plain `dict`; previously only the top-level keys were sorted while nested tables, inline tables, arrays of tables and inline tables inside an array kept their original order. ([#614](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/issues/614))\n-- Allow `Table.setdefault()` and `InlineTable.setdefault()` to retrieve existing values without supplying a default, matching document and mapping behavior.\n-\n-- Fix `item()` and `dumps()` writing a `datetime` whose UTC offset is not a whole number of minutes (e.g. the historical LMT offsets `zoneinfo` gives, such as `-00:44:30`) as invalid TOML like `1900-01-01T12:00:00Z:30`, which no parser accepts. Such a value is now written as the same instant in UTC; this also covers `DateTime.replace()` and `astimezone()`.\n-- Allow `DateTime.astimezone()` to use the local timezone when no timezone argument is supplied, matching `datetime.datetime`.\n-- Arithmetic and `replace()` results for `Integer`, `Float`, `String`, `DateTime`, `Date` and `Time` no longer share the original item's `Trivia`, so changing the result's comment or indentation no longer rewrites the item still stored in the document.\n+- Allow `Table.setdefault()` and `InlineTable.setdefault()` to retrieve existing values without supplying a default, matching document and mapping behavior. ([#710](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/710))\n+- Fix `item()` and `dumps()` writing a `datetime` whose UTC offset is not a whole number of minutes (e.g. the historical LMT offsets `zoneinfo` gives, such as `-00:44:30`) as invalid TOML like `1900-01-01T12:00:00Z:30`, which no parser accepts. Such a value is now written as the same instant in UTC; this also covers `DateTime.replace()` and `astimezone()`. ([#701](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/701))\n+- Allow `DateTime.astimezone()` to use the local timezone when no timezone argument is supplied, matching `datetime.datetime`. ([#651](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/651))\n+- Arithmetic and `replace()` results for `Integer`, `Float`, `String`, `DateTime`, `Date` and `Time` no longer share the original item's `Trivia`, so changing the result's comment or indentation no longer rewrites the item still stored in the document. ([#683](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/683))\n+- Fix `round()` on a `Float` without `ndigits` returning a `Float` (e.g. `2.0`) instead of an `Integer`, matching `round()` on a plain `float`. ([#695](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/695))\n+- Fix a regression in 0.15.1 where `string(..., multiline=True, escape=False)` added an extra newline to a value starting with a newline, making it impossible to write such a raw string verbatim; with `escape=False` the value is now used as given again. ([#655](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/issues/655))\n+- Preserve single-line literal quotes when replacing a table field with a plain string, falling back to basic quoting when the value requires escaping. ([#325](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/issues/325))\n+- Fix invalid output after deleting the last key under a dotted key inside an inline table; the emptied table now renders as `b = {}`. ([#664](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/664))\n+- Fix valid TOML being rejected as a duplicate when an out-of-order table header extends a table built from several dotted keys, e.g. `[a]` with `b.c = 1` and `b.d = 2`, then `[a.b.e]` after another table. ([#632](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/issues/632))\n - Fix an `AttributeError` when a table is defined out of order under an indented header nested four or more levels deep, e.g. ` [a.b.c.d]` then `[a.b.c]`. ([#663](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/663))\n+- Fix an out-of-order table being moved when it is separated from its sibling by an array of tables (e.g. `[tool.poetry]`, `[[plugins]]`, `[tool.other]`), so the document no longer round-trips unchanged. ([#702](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/702))\n+- Fix `update()` on an out-of-order table dropping sibling keys stored in its other fragments when one of the updated keys appears in a later fragment. ([#675](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/issues/675))\n+- Fix deleting, popping or replacing a key that was newly added to an out-of-order table. ([#699](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/699))\n+- Fix `TOMLDocument.value` and comparisons keeping only the last fragment of an array of tables split by other tables; all entries are now included, matching `unwrap()`. ([#697](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/697))\n+- Fix assigning plain dicts to a slice of an array of tables (e.g. `doc[\"a\"][:1] = [{\"x\": 4}]`) producing invalid output and leaving `unwrap()` and `json.dumps()` out of sync; an extended slice of the wrong length now raises before changing the document. ([#631](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/631))\n+- Assigning a value that is not a table to an item or slice of an array of tables now raises `ValueError` before changing the document. ([#712](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/712))\n+- Fix a `RecursionError` when parsing a dotted key at the maximum nesting depth followed by another key under the same prefix; `Container`, `Table` and `InlineTable` now implement `__deepcopy__`, and errors while assembling tables are reported as `ParseError`. ([#714](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/issues/714))\n+- Custom encoders registered with `register_encoder()` now receive only the `_parent` and `_sort_keys` keyword arguments they declare (or both when they accept `**kwargs`); previously an encoder declaring `_parent` but not `_sort_keys` failed with `TypeError`, and one declaring only `_sort_keys` never received it. ([#698](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/698))\n \n ## [0.15.2] - 2026-10-16\n \n@@ -30,7 +47,6 @@\n \n ### Fixed\n \n-- Fix invalid output after deleting the last key under a dotted key inside an inline table; the emptied table now renders as `b = {}`. ([#664](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/664))\n - Fix valid TOML being rejected when an out-of-order table reopens an implicit super-table with a dotted key: `[a.b.c]` then `[a]` with `b.z = 1` extends the implicit `a.b` super-table rather than redefining it (stdlib `tomllib` accepts it), so it now parses and round-trips instead of raising `Redefinition of an existing table`. The concrete-table case (`[a.b]` then `[a]` `b.z = 1`) stays rejected. ([#565](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/565))\n - Fix uppercase `E` exponent after a leading-zero mantissa (e.g. `0E2`) being rejected as an invalid number while `0e2` parsed fine. ([#586](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/586))\n - Fix non-lowercase special floats (e.g. `Inf`, `NaN`, `-INF`) being accepted; TOML only allows lowercase `inf` and `nan`, so they now raise `ParseError`. ([#628](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/628))\n@@ -69,7 +85,6 @@\n \n ### Fixed\n \n-- Preserve single-line literal quotes when replacing a table field with a plain string, falling back to basic quoting when the value requires escaping. ([#325](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/issues/325))\n - Fix `string()` dropping a leading newline of a multiline string on round-trip: a value beginning with a newline is now rendered with an extra leading newline (the one the parser trims after the opening delimiter) so it survives re-parsing.\n - Fix invalid serialization with a duplicated comma when removing a non-edge element from a parsed inline table. ([#486](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/486))\n - Fix invalid serialization with a duplicated comma when appending or inserting into a comma-first formatted array. ([#499](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/499))\n@@ -551,7 +566,8 @@\n - Fixed handling of super tables with different sections.\n - Fixed raw strings escaping.\n \n-[unreleased]: https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/compare/0.15.2...master\n+[unreleased]: https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/compare/0.15.3...master\n+[0.15.3]: https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/releases/tag/0.15.3\n [0.15.2]: https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/releases/tag/0.15.2\n [0.15.1]: https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/releases/tag/0.15.1\n [0.15.0]: https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/releases/tag/0.15.0\ndiff --git a/pyproject.toml b/pyproject.toml\nindex c9e1a86a..6805be98 100644\n--- a/pyproject.toml\n+++ b/pyproject.toml\n@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@\n [project]\n name = \"tomlkit\"\n-version = \"0.15.2\"\n+version = \"0.15.3\"\n description = \"Style preserving TOML library\"\n authors = [\n     { name = \"Sébastien Eustace\", email = \"sebastien@eustace.io\" },\ndiff --git a/tomlkit/__init__.py b/tomlkit/__init__.py\nindex 420c1751..7a233554 100644\n--- a/tomlkit/__init__.py\n+++ b/tomlkit/__init__.py\n@@ -27,7 +27,7 @@\n from tomlkit.api import ws\n \n \n-__version__ = \"0.15.2\"\n+__version__ = \"0.15.3\"\n __all__ = [\n     \"TOMLDocument\",\n     \"aot\",\ndiff --git a/uv.lock b/uv.lock\nindex b23c1d65..baf27c8d 100644\n--- a/uv.lock\n+++ b/uv.lock\n@@ -1550,7 +1550,7 @@ wheels = [\n \n [[package]]\n name = \"tomlkit\"\n-version = \"0.15.2\"\n+version = \"0.15.3\"\n source = { editable = \".\" }\n \n [package.dev-dependencies]\n# Change Log\n\n## [Unreleased]\n\n## [0.15.3] - 2026-11-24\n\n### Changed\n\n- Speed up looking up and replacing keys in tables: string lookups no longer build a temporary key, and replacing an existing value no longer scans every key in the table, which made updating many keys of a large table quadratic. ([#704](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/704))\n- Speed up repeated array appends by keeping existing indexes instead of rebuilding them. ([#666](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/666))\n- Speed up creating string values and keys, e.g. when building a document from Python data and dumping it: strings are escaped in one pass instead of per character, and the escape and bare-key character sets are built once. ([#709](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/709))\n- `comment()`, `Item.comment()` and `Array.add_line(..., comment=...)` now raise `ValueError` for control characters that TOML forbids in comments (anything but tab, plus `DEL`), including a bare carriage return; `comment()` still accepts LF and CRLF line breaks. Previously such comments were written out and produced a document that could not be parsed back. ([#705](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/705))\n- `date()` now raises `ValueError` when given a datetime string such as `\"1979-05-13T12:34:56\"` instead of returning a datetime. ([#673](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/673))\n- `Array.sort()` now reorders the serialized values too, keeping the array's formatting and comments in place; previously `list.sort()` only reordered the Python list, so `dumps()` still wrote the old order. ([#644](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/644))\n\n### Fixed\n\n- `dumps(..., sort_keys=True)` now sorts the keys of a parsed document recursively, matching the behavior on a plain `dict`; previously only the top-level keys were sorted while nested tables, inline tables, arrays of tables and inline tables inside an array kept their original order. ([#614](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/issues/614))\n- Allow `Table.setdefault()` and `InlineTable.setdefault()` to retrieve existing values without supplying a default, matching document and mapping behavior. ([#710](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/710))\n- Fix `item()` and `dumps()` writing a `datetime` whose UTC offset is not a whole number of minutes (e.g. the historical LMT offsets `zoneinfo` gives, such as `-00:44:30`) as invalid TOML like `1900-01-01T12:00:00Z:30`, which no parser accepts. Such a value is now written as the same instant in UTC; this also covers `DateTime.replace()` and `astimezone()`. ([#701](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/701))\n- Allow `DateTime.astimezone()` to use the local timezone when no timezone argument is supplied, matching `datetime.datetime`. ([#651](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/651))\n- Arithmetic and `replace()` results for `Integer`, `Float`, `String`, `DateTime`, `Date` and `Time` no longer share the original item's `Trivia`, so changing the result's comment or indentation no longer rewrites the item still stored in the document. ([#683](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/683))\n- Fix `round()` on a `Float` without `ndigits` returning a `Float` (e.g. `2.0`) instead of an `Integer`, matching `round()` on a plain `float`. ([#695](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/695))\n- Fix a regression in 0.15.1 where `string(..., multiline=True, escape=False)` added an extra newline to a value starting with a newline, making it impossible to write such a raw string verbatim; with `escape=False` the value is now used as given again. ([#655](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/issues/655))\n- Preserve single-line literal quotes when replacing a table field with a plain string, falling back to basic quoting when the value requires escaping. ([#325](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/issues/325))\n- Fix invalid output after deleting the last key under a dotted key inside an inline table; the emptied table now renders as `b = {}`. ([#664](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/664))\n- Fix valid TOML being rejected as a duplicate when an out-of-order table header extends a table built from several dotted keys, e.g. `[a]` with `b.c = 1` and `b.d = 2`, then `[a.b.e]` after another table. ([#632](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/issues/632))\n- Fix an `AttributeError` when a table is defined out of order under an indented header nested four or more levels deep, e.g. ` [a.b.c.d]` then `[a.b.c]`. ([#663](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/663))\n- Fix an out-of-order table being moved when it is separated from its sibling by an array of tables (e.g. `[tool.poetry]`, `[[plugins]]`, `[tool.other]`), so the document no longer round-trips unchanged. ([#702](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/702))\n- Fix `update()` on an out-of-order table dropping sibling keys stored in its other fragments when one of the updated keys appears in a later fragment. ([#675](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/issues/675))\n- Fix deleting, popping or replacing a key that was newly added to an out-of-order table. ([#699](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/699))\n- Fix `TOMLDocument.value` and comparisons keeping only the last fragment of an array of tables split by other tables; all entries are now included, matching `unwrap()`. ([#697](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/697))\n- Fix assigning plain dicts to a slice of an array of tables (e.g. `doc[\"a\"][:1] = [{\"x\": 4}]`) producing invalid output and leaving `unwrap()` and `json.dumps()` out of sync; an extended slice of the wrong length now raises before changing the document. ([#631](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/631))\n- Assigning a value that is not a table to an item or slice of an array of tables now raises `ValueError` before changing the document. ([#712](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/712))\n- Fix a `RecursionError` when parsing a dotted key at the maximum nesting depth followed by another key under the same prefix; `Container`, `Table` and `InlineTable` now implement `__deepcopy__`, and errors while assembling tables are reported as `ParseError`. ([#714](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/issues/714))\n- Custom encoders registered with `register_encoder()` now receive only the `_parent` and `_sort_keys` keyword arguments they declare (or both when they accept `**kwargs`); previously an encoder declaring `_parent` but not `_sort_keys` failed with `TypeError`, and one declaring only `_sort_keys` never received it. ([#698](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/698))\n\n## [0.15.2] - 2026-10-16\n\n### Changed\n\n- Write the ESC control character as `\\u001b` instead of `\\e`, which is only valid in TOML 1.1, so the output stays readable by TOML 1.0 parsers such as `tomllib`. ([#641](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/641))\n- `key_value()` now raises `UnexpectedCharError` on anything other than whitespace or a comment after the pair, instead of silently discarding it (e.g. `key_value(\"a = 1 b = 2\")`), matching `parse()`. ([#594](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/594))\n- `integer()` given a string now validates it against the TOML integer grammar and keeps the original text, so grouping underscores (e.g. `integer(\"1_000\")`) survive `dumps()`; strings that are not valid TOML integers (e.g. `\"010\"`) now raise `ValueError`. ([#336](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/issues/336))\n- Add a `fold` argument to `DateTime` and `Time`, mirroring the stdlib, and carry `fold` through `item()`, arithmetic (including datetime subtraction) and `unwrap()`, so a folded local time no longer converts an hour off. ([#619](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/issues/619), [#623](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/623), [#626](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/626))\n- Declare the project metadata in the PEP 621 `[project]` table; building from source now requires `poetry-core>=2.2.0`. ([#607](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/607), [#609](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/609))\n\n### Fixed\n\n- Fix valid TOML being rejected when an out-of-order table reopens an implicit super-table with a dotted key: `[a.b.c]` then `[a]` with `b.z = 1` extends the implicit `a.b` super-table rather than redefining it (stdlib `tomllib` accepts it), so it now parses and round-trips instead of raising `Redefinition of an existing table`. The concrete-table case (`[a.b]` then `[a]` `b.z = 1`) stays rejected. ([#565](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/565))\n- Fix uppercase `E` exponent after a leading-zero mantissa (e.g. `0E2`) being rejected as an invalid number while `0e2` parsed fine. ([#586](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/586))\n- Fix non-lowercase special floats (e.g. `Inf`, `NaN`, `-INF`) being accepted; TOML only allows lowercase `inf` and `nan`, so they now raise `ParseError`. ([#628](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/628))\n- Fix parse errors reporting the wrong line and column in documents with CRLF or mixed line endings. ([#642](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/642))\n- Fix `item()` reordering the keys of an inline table (dict-valued keys were forced last) under the default `sort_keys=False`. ([#546](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/issues/546))\n- Fix `unwrap()` moving a key to the end after its value was replaced (e.g. `doc[\"b\"] = 9`), while `dumps()` and `keys()` kept the original order. ([#591](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/591))\n- Fix appending a key to a parsed inline table that uses `\", \"` separators emitting a bare `\",\"` for the new entry, leaving the table inconsistently spaced (e.g. `{x = 1, y = 2,z = 3}`). ([#595](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/595))\n- Fix an emptied array of tables being dropped from the output: it now renders as `key = []`, placed and keyed relative to the nearest table header so it parses back into the same table. ([#567](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/567))\n- Fix a single-line array whose last element is a trailing comment (e.g. from `add_line(value, comment=...)`) rendering its closing `]` on the comment line, producing unparseable output. ([#580](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/issues/580))\n- Fix `del array[start:stop:step]` with a negative or omitted bound removing the wrong elements from the rendered output. ([#599](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/599))\n- Fix array slice assignment mutating the array before raising `ValueError(\"slice assignment is not supported\")`. ([#600](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/600))\n- Fix `String.__add__` splicing the appended text into a basic string without escaping it, so appending a quote or backslash produced invalid TOML. ([#612](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/612))\n- Fix a bare carriage return in a multiline string producing invalid TOML: it is now escaped as `\\r` in a multiline basic string and rejected with `InvalidStringError` in a multiline literal string; CRLF line endings are left intact. ([#539](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/539))\n- Fix a tz-aware `datetime.time` rendering with a UTC offset (e.g. `07:32:00+02:00`), which TOML local times do not allow; it now renders as a local time. ([#613](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/613))\n- Fix arithmetic on a signed float producing `+-0.0` (e.g. `-1.5` times `0`), which does not parse. ([#629](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/629))\n- Fix two `Bool` items never comparing equal to each other; they now compare by value. ([#660](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/660))\n\n## [0.15.1] - 2026-07-17\n\n### Changed\n\n- Speed up membership tests (`key in ...`) on `Container`, `Table` and `InlineTable` with native `__contains__` implementations, avoiding the inherited `MutableMapping` round-trip through `__getitem__` (which resolves the value and builds an exception on every absent key). ([#483](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/issues/483))\n- Speed up parsing by making `Source` index-based: it now tracks an integer position over the input string instead of materializing a list of `(index, char)` tuples up front, so construction is O(1) and state save/restore no longer copies an iterator. ([#489](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/489))\n- Speed up parsing by scanning character runs in bulk: `Source.advance_while`/`advance_until` consume a whole run of whitespace, bare-key or number characters in a single pass over the input string instead of one `inc()` call per character. ([#490](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/490))\n- Speed up parsing of single-line strings by bulk-appending the run of ordinary characters up to the next delimiter, backslash or control character in one pass, instead of one character at a time. ([#491](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/491))\n- Speed up parsing by removing the internal `TOMLChar` wrapper: the parser now reads plain `str` characters from `Source` and detects end-of-input positionally, avoiding a per-character object construction and method dispatch. ([#492](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/492))\n- Speed up parsing by comparing `StringType` members by identity (`is`) instead of building a set on every `is_basic`/`is_literal`/`is_singleline`/`is_multiline` call, avoiding millions of enum hashes while parsing. ([#502](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/502))\n- Speed up merging super tables by merging in place instead of deep-copying the growing target on every merge, turning the parse of documents with many subtables under a shared super table (e.g. consecutive `[a.b.c]` / `[a.b.d]` headers) from O(n²) into O(n). ([#503](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/503))\n- Speed up membership tests (`key in ...`) on out-of-order tables with a native `OutOfOrderTableProxy.__contains__`, completing [#483](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/issues/483) for the last mapping type that still inherited the slow `MutableMapping` mixin (which resolves the value and builds an exception on every absent key). ([#515](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/515))\n- Speed up parsing documents with many dotted keys or table headers sharing a prefix by validating out-of-order tables incrementally: each new fragment is merged into a cached validation container once, instead of re-merging (and deep-copying) every earlier fragment on each append, turning a super-cubic worst case into linear time (80 shared-prefix dotted keys: ~8 s → ~10 ms). ([#479](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/issues/479))\n- Speed up parsing of arrays that close right after a value (e.g. the `files = [...]` blocks that dominate lock files): the parser no longer attempts to read a value while sitting on the closing `]`, which previously built an `UnexpectedCharError` just to discard it — and constructing that exception eagerly computes a line/column by scanning the whole document, making it O(document size) per such array. ([#517](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/517))\n- Speed up parsing of multiline strings by bulk-appending the run of ordinary characters — across raw line feeds and tabs — up to the next delimiter, backslash, carriage return or control character, instead of one character at a time. This extends to `\"\"\"`/`'''` bodies the single-line fast path added in [#491](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/491); a `\\r` still stops the scan so `\\r\\n` stays validated and byte-for-byte preserved. ([#518](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/518))\n- Speed up `unwrap()` (converting a parsed document to a plain `dict`) by resolving each key directly from the container's key map instead of iterating the inherited `MutableMapping` view, which rebuilt a `SingleKey` from the bare string for every key just to re-look-up the value. Out-of-order tables still resolve through their proxy, so their validation is unchanged. ([#521](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/521))\n- Speed up rendering (`as_string()` / `dumps()`) of inline tables with many keys by precomputing the last-key and last-deleted-element indices in a single pass, instead of rescanning the remaining body on every separator comma — turning an O(n²) render into O(n). ([#525](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/525))\n- Raise on malformed array element instead of dropping it, ([#527](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/527))\n\n### Fixed\n\n- Fix `string()` dropping a leading newline of a multiline string on round-trip: a value beginning with a newline is now rendered with an extra leading newline (the one the parser trims after the opening delimiter) so it survives re-parsing.\n- Fix invalid serialization with a duplicated comma when removing a non-edge element from a parsed inline table. ([#486](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/486))\n- Fix invalid serialization with a duplicated comma when appending or inserting into a comma-first formatted array. ([#499](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/499))\n- Fix `ParseError` when a sub-table extends the last element of an array of tables after an unrelated table. ([#261](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/issues/261))\n- Fix unparseable serialization when adding a key to a dotted-key table inside an inline table. ([#500](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/500))\n- Fix a table replaced by a plain value being serialized inside the preceding table's body when other tables follow; the value now moves before the first table like other root-level values. ([#504](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/issues/504))\n- Fix assigning a table over a dotted key (e.g. `doc[\"a\"] = {...}` where `a` came from `a.b = ...`): the dotted prefix was duplicated onto the new `[a]` header, and the header then swallowed any sibling that follows it on round-trip. The replacement now renders as a plain table and, when needed, moves before the inline entries (values and dotted keys) it would otherwise capture. ([#513](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/issues/513), [#524](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/issues/524))\n- Restore `dumps()` rendering mapping-like wrappers around a parsed document (e.g. `dotty_dict`'s `Dotty`) through their delegated `as_string`, preserving the original table order and layout instead of re-encoding through a plain dict — a 0.15.0 regression. ([#482](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/issues/482))\n- Fix uncontrolled recursion when parsing deeply nested documents: crafted input could crash the process with a `RecursionError`. Values nested more than 100 levels deep and keys with more than 100 dotted fragments now raise `ParseError`. ([#459](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/issues/459))\n- Fix `comment()` producing invalid TOML for a multiline string by prefixing every line with `#`, not just the first. ([#449](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/issues/449))\n- Fix the separator comma being swallowed by a trailing comment when appending a key to a multiline inline table, leaving the new key without a separator so the result no longer round-trips. ([#512](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/issues/512))\n- Fix a `KeyAlreadyPresent` error when parsing or accessing an out-of-order table whose array-of-tables elements are split across the table's parts. ([#505](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/issues/505))\n- Out-of-order value-vs-table and dotted-key-vs-table redefinitions are now rejected at parse time instead of being silently accepted or raising only on access. The parser also detects when a non-dotted key is a prefix of an existing dotted key, matching the stdlib `tomllib` behaviour. ([#523](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/issues/523))\n- Reject tables inserted into inline tables instead of serializing invalid TOML. ([#531](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/issues/531))\n- Fix assigning an array of tables over a dotted key (e.g. `doc[\"a\"] = aot(...)` where `a` came from `a.b = ...`): the new `[[a]]` header kept the dotted key's inline position and swallowed the following dotted sibling on round-trip. The array of tables now renders past the inline entries it would otherwise capture, mirroring the table fix for [#513](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/issues/513). ([#542](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/issues/542))\n- Fix a new top-level scalar being captured by a table rendered from a dotted key: appending a scalar after a dotted-key entry (e.g. `a.b = 1`) whose table had gained a `[a.c]`-style child placed the scalar inside that table's scope, silently re-nesting it on round-trip. Scalars now move before such an entry, like they do before regular tables. ([#543](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/issues/543))\n- Fix invalid serialization with a duplicated `[table]` header when adding a key to an out-of-order table whose concrete header is declared after its sub-tables; the new key now lands in the existing concrete part instead of giving the header-less super part a second header. ([#545](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/545))\n- Fix a table's display name (its exact header spelling, including whitespace and quoting) being normalised when the table is assigned onto itself, e.g. `doc[k] = doc[k]` rewriting `[keys .'a'.'c']` to `[keys.a.'c']`. ([#291](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/issues/291))\n- Fix missing newlines when appending a key after a dotted inline table, including when the original document has no trailing newline. ([#533](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/533))\n- Preserve trailing whitespace when replacing a super table, including assigning it onto itself. ([#534](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/534))\n- Fix `str()` and `repr()` of out-of-order table proxies to show their merged values. ([#536](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/536))\n- Reject decimal integer literals that exceed Python's integer-string conversion limit instead of coercing them to infinity. ([#538](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/538))\n# Open (Unmerged) Pull Requests on `python-poetry/tomlkit` as of 2026-11-25\n\nCaptured verbatim from `github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit` (`state: open`; NOT included in 0.15.3 release commit `d2aa305`).\n\n## PR #721: fix: decode bytes strictly as UTF-8 when parsing (#720)\n- State: `open` (unmerged; updated `2026-11-25T10:12:15Z`)\n- URL: https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/721\n\n### Summary\n\nFixes #720\n\nWhen parsing bytes via `tomlkit.parse`, `tomlkit.loads`, or `tomlkit.load` on a binary stream, `Parser.__init__` previously called `tomlkit._compat.decode()`, which falls back across `[\"utf-8\", \"latin1\", \"ascii\"]`. Because latin-1 accepts any byte sequence without error, invalid UTF-8 bytes were silently accepted and produced mojibake instead of raising an error.\n\nThe TOML specification mandates that TOML documents are encoded in UTF-8 (matching `tomllib` / `tomli` behavior).\n\n### Changes\n- In `tomlkit/parser.py`: decode `bytes` strictly as UTF-8 in `Parser.__init__` via `string.decode(\"utf-8\")`.\n- In `tests/test_api.py`: add unit tests verifying `parse()`, `loads()`, and `load()` raise `UnicodeDecodeError` on invalid UTF-8 bytes and parse valid UTF-8 bytes properly.\n- In `tests/test_toml_tests.py`: add `test_invalid_encode_bytes` testing `invalid/encoding/*` cases with binary file reading (`\"rb\"`).\n\n## PR #635: Keep out-of-order table indices valid after a table is removed\n- State: `open` (unmerged; updated `2026-11-17T04:44:45Z`)\n- URL: https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/635\n\n## Summary\n\nDeleting two keys through the same out-of-order table proxy raises or silently does nothing:\n\n```python\nsrc = '[tool.black]\\nline-length = 88\\n\\n[project]\\nname = \"x\"\\n\\n[tool.ruff]\\nselect = [\"E\"]\\n'\ndoc = tomlkit.parse(src); tool = doc[\"tool\"]\ndel tool[\"black\"]; del tool[\"ruff\"]      # IndexError: list index out of range\ntomlkit.parse(src)[\"tool\"].clear()        # IndexError\n```\n\nWith `[tool.a]`, `[tool.b]` and `[tool.c]` split by other tables, `clear()` returns but leaves `[tool.b]` and `[tool.c]` in the output. `_tables_map` holds positions in `self._tables`, and `_remove_table` removed the table with `list.remove` without shifting the later positions (`list.remove` also compares by equality, so it could take an equal empty table). It now removes the table by identity and shifts the later positions down by one.\n\n`test_delete_keys_through_the_same_out_of_order_table` fails on master; dropping the shift or shifting the wrong side fails it too. `pytest tests` (1,069 passed) and `pre-commit run` on the changed files pass.\n\n## Agent Drafting Metadata\n\n- Agent: Claude Code\n- Model: Claude\n- Notes: Found by comparing edits against a tomllib model. I reviewed the change and\n\n## PR #707: Fix serialization of dates and times created by factory methods\n- State: `open` (unmerged; updated `2026-11-09T04:13:30Z`)\n- URL: https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/707\n\n## Summary\n\n`Date.fromisoformat()`, `Date.fromordinal()` and the other inherited date factories return TOML items with an empty `_raw` value. `Time.fromisoformat()` does the same. Serializing one produces `value = \\n`, which both Tomlkit and stdlib `tomllib` reject.\n\nWhen no source text was supplied, generate the date's ISO text or use the existing local-time formatter. This follows the fallback already used by `DateTime`; parsed items retain their original text and comments.\n\nFifteen regressions cover date/time factories, fractional seconds, existing raw formatting and the unchanged DateTime behavior. On Python 3.11+, serialization is checked with the independent stdlib parser as well as Tomlkit. Before the fix: 11 failed, 4 passed. After the fix: all pass.\n\nValidation on Windows / Python 3.13.4:\n- Full suite including the pinned toml-test submodule: **1,449 passed**.\n- All six configured pre-commit hooks: passed.\n- New test file Mypy: passed. Full-tree Mypy reports the same 33 existing diagnostics on both base and patch.\n\n## Duplicate Check\n\n- [x] I searched the open PRs and found none that already fixes this issue.\n- Related open PRs: #652 routes reflected addition through the w\n\n## PR #706: Add a multiline array option to dump and dumps\n- State: `open` (unmerged; updated `2026-11-07T23:03:32Z`)\n- URL: https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/706\n\n## Summary\n\nAdd `multiline=True` to `dumps()` and `dump()` so callers can render every array one item per line without traversing and changing the document first:\n\n```python\ntomlkit.dumps({\"ports\": [8001, 8002]}, multiline=True)\n# ports = [\n#     8001,\n#     8002,\n# ]\n```\n\nThe option reaches arrays inside tables, inline tables, arrays of tables and other arrays. It uses the existing `Array.multiline(True)` formatting and preserves comments, document layout outside arrays and input objects. The default preserves existing formatting, including explicitly multiline arrays. Empty arrays stay empty.\n\nPass the option through internal render methods. Custom `as_string()` methods retain their no-argument interface and control their output. There is no shared formatting state. This implements the boolean option requested in #385; item-count and line-width selection are not added.\n\nFixes #385.\n\nValidation on Linux / Python 3.12.12:\n\n- 18 new tests fail against the original source because the option is unavailable; all pass with the change. Covers nested arrays, comments, aliases, custom renderers/encoders, reentrant calls, exceptions and concurrent renders.\n- Full suite: 1,452 passing, inclu\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
